---
description: Route to a workflow and use ordinary English
alwaysApply: true
---

When these skills are installed, route every request through the catalog
workflow unless the user explicitly says to skip that routing, or the request
is obviously outside what these skills apply to. Invoke
`~/.cursor/skills/workflows/SKILL.md`. Front doors: foggy → explore; concrete →
define, which interviews for alignment, then classifies and binds a workflow.
A short description starts that interview; it does not approve the plan. A
reply that finishes a skill ends with the exact `## Next` block
(`/<skill> <KEY>` — why). An open alignment question does not include that
block. Do not freestyle past a supported workflow.

On Cursor (Desktop, Cloud, CLI, Mobile), every Task spawn of any type —
including computerUse and videoReview — must pass an explicit `model` slug
from the Cursor Models allowlist only: `composer-2.5` (Routine/Moderate) or
`cursor-grok-4.6-high` (Demanding/manager). Only `composer-*` and
`cursor-grok-*` slugs are provably first-party; bare `grok-*` and picker
slugs bill Other Models. If the chosen slug is absent from the Task enum,
pass the other allowlisted slug, else `composer-2.5`. Never inherit, omit
model, or pick a picker slug. No `*-fast` variants. Load
`~/.cursor/skills/concepts/CONCEPT_DELEGATION.md` and
`~/.cursor/skills/concepts/platforms/cursor.md` before every spawn.

Language: before any reply the operator will see, read
`~/.cursor/skills/concepts/CONCEPT_LANGUAGE.md`,
`~/.cursor/skills/concepts/LANGUAGE-PHRASES.md`, and
`~/.cursor/skills/concepts/LANGUAGE-HUMANIZER.md`. Follow those files. Spell
names in full (`GeneralProcessSimulator`, not `GPS`). Keep **harness** for the
agent host (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, …). Do not call a sandbox tree, wrapper,
or other code a harness.
